{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "7b3d3619-e1a4-454d-a357-e170e5d330e0",
    "name": "Exponentor Analyzer Agents",
    "description": "All endpoints of the `analyzer` service (see API_GUIDE.md).\n\n**Setup:** import `Exponentor_Analyzer.postman_environment.json` too and select it.\n\n**How variables work:** every body reads its values from the environment. A collection script exposes each environment value as `{{json_<name>}}` (arrays/objects as-is, text quoted), and each request's test script writes its results back to the environment, so the next request picks them up.\n\n**Suggested order (or use Run collection):** Health -> Prerequisites -> Profile -> Roadmap -> Generate paper -> Run code -> Grade written answer -> Grade submission -> Match explanation.\n\nAI calls can take 30-120 s; keep Postman's request timeout at 0 (no limit) or at least 300000 ms.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Runs before every request.",
          "// 1. Make sure an environment is selected (the test scripts save their results into it).",
          "if (!pm.environment.name) {",
          "    throw new Error(\"Select the 'Exponentor Analyzer - Local' environment (top right) before sending requests.\");",
          "}",
          "",
          "// 2. Expose every environment value as {{json_<name>}} so request bodies stay valid JSON:",
          "//    arrays/objects are inserted as they are, everything else is inserted as a quoted JSON string.",
          "//    Numbers in bodies use the plain {{name}} form instead.",
          "const env = pm.environment.toObject();",
          "Object.keys(env).forEach(function (key) {",
          "    const value = env[key];",
          "    let out = JSON.stringify(value === undefined || value === null ? \"\" : String(value));",
          "    if (typeof value === \"string\") {",
          "        try {",
          "            const parsed = JSON.parse(value);",
          "            if (parsed !== null && typeof parsed === \"object\") out = value;",
          "        } catch (e) { /* plain text */ }",
          "    } else if (value !== null && typeof value === \"object\") {",
          "        out = JSON.stringify(value);",
          "    }",
          "    pm.variables.set(\"json_\" + key, out);",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Runs after every request.",
          "pm.test(\"Status is 2xx\", function () {",
          "    pm.expect(pm.response.code, pm.response.text()).to.be.within(200, 299);",
          "});",
          "console.log(pm.info.requestName + \" -> \" + pm.response.code + \" in \" + pm.response.responseTime + \" ms\");"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
